# A PDF form in the viewer (tools/pdf-make-form-tests.py): its text and
# choice fields are the viewer's own controls over the page, with the
# document's values in them; typing changes the value the document holds;
# a check box is drawn by the page and pressed through the viewer, and the
# page's picture follows; the download is the document with the values in
# it (an update appended to the file, which opens as a PDF again).
# The page is 400 x 400 at automatic zoom 1.25 in a 900 x 700 window:
# a point (x, y) of the page is at (200 + 1.25 x, 142 + 1.25 (400 - y)).
downloads-folder
resize 900 700
open pdf-form.pdf
advance 500 6
assert-title pdf-form.pdf
# The text field holds the document's value, the combo box its choice.
assert-value field-10-0 Hello
assert-value field-18-0 g
# The check box's Yes appearance (blue) and the radio group's B (red) are
# drawn by the page; the hidden field is not shown.
assert-pixel 519 261 #0000ff
assert-pixel 644 261 #ff0000
# Typing into the text field changes what the document holds.
click 300 194
key end
type , there
advance 400 3
assert-value field-10-0 Hello, there
# Pressing the check box turns it off, and the page's picture is drawn again.
click 519 261
advance 500 6
assert-pixel 519 261 #b3b3b3
# Pressing radio A: A on (red), B off (gray).
click 582 261
advance 500 6
assert-pixel 582 261 #ff0000
assert-pixel 644 261 #b3b3b3
# The download is the document with the values in it, larger than the file.
click 832 99
advance 300 3
assert-status Downloaded pdf-form.pdf
assert-download pdf-form.pdf 5200 %%EOF
